These fictional policy records already have checked product and current-status fields. The code chooses the record for the requested product that is marked current.

```javascript
const policies = [
  { id: "A", product: "mug", current: false },
  { id: "B", product: "mug", current: true }
];
const match = policies.find(p => p.product === "mug" && p.current);
console.log(match.id);
```

It prints B, even though A came first.
